<title>AUSTRIA: Nigeria says thinks OPEC will keep present ceiling.</title>
<headline>Nigeria says thinks OPEC will keep present ceiling.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigerian oil minister Dan Etete said on Monday that OPEC was likely to keep its current quotas at its meeting due to start on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We will keep the quotas, I don't think anyone wants a change,&quot; Etete told lobby reporters on his arrival here.</p>
<p>He said he did not think OPEC was overproducing and that he thought it could accomodate additional Iraqi oil.</p>
<p>&quot;Of course, obviously,&quot; he said when asked if OPEC could accomodate Iraqi output.  </p>
<p>Etete was speaking shortly after Iraqi ambassador to the U.N. Nizar Hamdoon said in New York that his country had agreed to U.N. conditions that had held up the oil-for-food deal.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +431 713 2034</p>
</text>
